  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Find the maximum value of $\\frac{1}{5+2\\cos x}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac13$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}-1&\\le\\cos x\\le1\\\\-2&\\le2\\cos x\\le2\\\\3&\\le5+2\\cos x\\le7\\end{align*}$$\nThe reciprocal is greatest when its positive denominator is smallest. Thus the maximum is $\\frac13$, attained when $\\cos x=-1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
